# agpkg manifest — required-tier software (docs/SYSTEM.md §6.1, M10).
# Format per line: <name> <url> <sha256>   ('#' comments, blank lines ok)
#
# The sha256 pins content, so transport honesty is not load-bearing — but
# the canonical source is GitHub releases. On networks where GitHub stalls,
# prefix the URL with https://gh-proxy.com/ (sha256 still verified).
#
# aginx v0.3.2 and aginx-carrier v0.1.0 musl assets shipped 2026-08-30 and
# are active below. aginxbrowser's musl asset is still pending — until its
# release pipeline ships it, aginxbrowser installs via adb + `agpkg install`.

aginx          https://github.com/yinnho/aginx/releases/download/v0.3.2/aginx-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl 1f8134d0d7bbead9ffcff9c7c1cb1499f3fcc10b4c7f3db7f44e41d658991690
aginx-carrier  https://github.com/yinnho/aginx-carrier/releases/download/v0.1.0/aginx-carrier-v0.1.0-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl 6fbf5c9cb73c5a3ab8b6e8c58dd5de0165499bed357eb1667054b33569be53d0

# aginxbrowser  https://github.com/yinnho/aginxbrowser/releases/download/v0.2.4/aginxbrowser-v0.2.4-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl <sha256 pending>
